                <pb facs="0879" n="767" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg767"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Moffat to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-12-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Moffat reports the unanimous election of Estrada and Diaz as president and
                    vice president respectively. He says there is intense enthusiasm.</p>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[To be continued in <ref target="frus:frus1911">Foreign Relations,
                        1911</ref>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
